{"game": "warframe", "language": "english", "appid": 230410, "month": "2022-09", "window": 2, "start_date": 1662595200, "end_date": 1663286399, "month_true_total": 2601, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-14 19:03:53 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "122298896", "author": {"steamid": "76561198063371220", "personaname": "Tridler", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Tridler/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 288490, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 198515, "last_played": 1785097497, "avatar": "d42eaad1b7e4e62b9431e812f2c106bc7bf36cfc"}, "language": "english", "review": "Best free to play game IMO. So much content, so so much content. There's a lot of grind, but that's just the nature of the game, it has its own charm. If you can find a group of friends to grind it together you'll have some of the greatest late night hangouts and conversations of your life. Although, there are a few items they should boost the drop rate on *cough* Arum Spinosa *cough* Ambassador *cough*.\n\nThere are common enough special events in-game there tends to be something to do even if you're at end game content, which on its own will take many many hours to get to. Updates aren't always the most polished, but for a free game it's more than good enough, it's downright great. Rather than release simple same-y content they take risks and add in new gamemodes and mechanics that shake things up. While true these changes can be unbalanced at first they usually pull things back in line in relatively short order. To be fair, they need to balance 9+ years of updates and mechanics, sometimes it's just going to be rough for a week or two while they get a new expansion in balance. Although, devs, balance the Laetum, it is way too strong IMO.\n\nBesides, I have a bit of a pet theory that they lean towards the difficult-new-expansion side of the balance on fresh release of new content to keep the crazy-chomping-at-the-bit players (like me) in check with a steep grind, only the pull it back as time goes on to add accessibility to more casual players. I believe this to be a good thing, gives the avid players a challenge but allows more casual players to stay involved, keeping the playerbase alive.\n\nLong story short, great game, lots of grind, lots of content.", "timestamp_created": 1663284706, "timestamp_updated": 1663284706, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.497737526893615723", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1364234640", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "122298531", "author": {"steamid": "76561198097173944", "personaname": "Toasted Popcorn", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/ToastedPopcornButCool/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 25, "playtime_forever": 13251, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 13251, "last_played": 1663032889, "avatar": "ed09c1f38f2e0f8ac20d47fe618f058822180ade"}, "language": "english", "review": "Staring in horror at my 200th attempt to get 1 single argon crystal", "timestamp_created": 1663283946, "timestamp_updated": 1663283946, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 8, "votes_funny": 7, "weighted_vote_score": "0.472344696521759033", "comment_count": 4, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1364234640", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 19, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "122298183", "author": {"steamid": "76561198174127690", "personaname": "King Y16", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Y16_King/", "num_games_owned": 539, "num_reviews": 4, "playtime_forever": 6878, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_re